The authorization model is correctly applied: the new `/admin/purge-user` endpoint is gated with `@require_role("admin")` (app/routes/admin.py:47), which satisfies policy §4 ("Every endpoint under /admin requires the admin role, enforced with @require_role('admin')") and §3 ("Only admins may delete or refund orders"). The `require_role` decorator (app/auth.py:69-85) correctly enforces ROLE_RANK >= admin and returns 401/403, so there is no missing or incorrect authorization on the changed endpoint.

The SQL injection present in the new code (app/routes/admin.py:54-57, `% username` string interpolation) is a CWE-89 violation of policy §5, but that is outside the authorization flaw classes (CWE-639/862/863) I am scoped to report.

